==============================================================================
COUNTEREXAMPLE (i) -- a SHARED blinding row
==============================================================================
Two claim sites, three published coordinates each.

 seed  disclosed dim (independent)   disclosed dim (shared)   marginals uniform?
    1                            0                        3     yes, each site 0
    2                            0                        3     yes, each site 0
    3                            0                        3     yes, each site 0
    5                            0                        3     yes, each site 0
    8                            0                        3     yes, each site 0
   13                            0                        3     yes, each site 0

  Reading: with a shared row each site's MARGINAL view is still
  perfectly blinded (disclosed 0 on its own), and the JOINT view
  discloses VIEW = 3 coordinates.  That is the project's known trap.

  What determines the witness, explicitly:
    V_0 - V_1 = (M_0 - M_1).w  = [23, 86, 87]   (blinding cancels)
    the other witness gives      [83, 73, 62]   -- separated
  -> the difference of the two sites' views is a function of w with
     no blinding left in it, whatever beta is.  [COMPUTED]

==============================================================================
COUNTEREXAMPLE (ii) -- ruling R-3: two DISTINCT rows, coinciding
VALUES
==============================================================================
The maps are the INDEPENDENT ones (two distinct symbols, disjoint
stream positions).  Only the VALUES drawn happen to coincide.

  seed 1: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True
  seed 2: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True
  seed 3: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True
  seed 5: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True
  seed 8: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True
  seed 13: gate's disclosed dimension = 0  (the honest answer); realised view leaks the witness functional: True; separated from w': True

  -> on 6/6 adversarial instances the gate reports
     'disclosed 0' and the realised view still determines
     (M_0 - M_1).w exactly.  The gate is a statement about the
     STRUCTURE (which symbol each site uses); the leak is a
     statement about the VALUES.  No rank computation can see it.

==============================================================================
PRICING: an accident versus a broken draw discipline
==============================================================================
  independent draws, k coordinates mod 101:
    k=1: predicted q^-k = 9.901e-03; measured over 400,000 trials = 1.014e-02 (4057 hits)
    k=2: predicted q^-k = 9.803e-05; measured over 400,000 trials = 1.075e-04 (43 hits)

  At the real geometry a blinding row is 256 Goldilocks words, so an
  ACCIDENTAL coincidence of two rows is p^-256 = 2^-16384 -- not a
  term anybody needs to carry.  [COMPUTED]

  A BROKEN DRAW DISCIPLINE is a different object entirely: if two
  roles read the SAME stream positions (a reused buffer, a cloned
  generator, an off-by-one in a draw count, a re-entered commit
  path), the coincidence has probability ONE and is invisible to
  every gate above.  That -- not the accident -- is what ruling R-3
  asks a draw-accounting test to exclude.

ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED.
